import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Surveillance Infrastructure Graph" path="/">
  <p>
    SIG is an open, vendor-agnostic, temporally versioned record of surveillance
    infrastructure — what is deployed, where and by whom, how it is connected and
    governed, and exactly which sources support or contradict every material claim.
    SIG <strong>reports</strong>; it does not endorse.
  </p>

  <h2>How to read this record</h2>
  <p>
    Every material claim on this site carries four independent epistemic fields, a
    support glyph that says <em>why</em> it is trusted, a persistent marker when a
    value is contested, and an honest, clickable gap wherever SIG has not (yet)
    looked. Absence of a row is <strong>not</strong> evidence of absence.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/visual-language/">The epistemic visual language</a> — the reference for every field, glyph, marker, and gap.</li>
    <li><a href="/reference-map/">Reference map</a> — with a full tabular equivalent (usable without JavaScript).</li>
    <li><a href="/reference-graph/">Reference graph</a> — with a full list equivalent (usable without JavaScript).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reproducible by design</h2>
  <p>
    Every page exposes a belief-pinned permalink and a citation you can hand to a
    council member or cite in a filing. A citation captured today re-resolves to the
    same belief even after SIG corrects itself. See the citation block below.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
